---
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage slug="tracking" lead="Katari sends your reading progress to tracking sites such as AniList and MyAnimeList.">
  <Callout label="Comics only" tone="warning">
    <p>For now only comics can be tracked. Books and video have no tracking, on any tracker.</p>
  </Callout>

  <Task id="log-in" title="Log in to a tracker">
    <ol>
      <li>Open <Path>Settings › Tracking</Path>.</li>
      <li>Tap a tracker and log in.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The trackers are MangaBaka, MyAnimeList, AniList, Kitsu, Shikimori, Bangumi, MangaUpdates, Hikka and Comick. A login belongs to the
      profile you're in, so each profile can use its own accounts.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="track" title="Track a title">
    <ol>
      <li>Open the title and tap <strong>Tracking</strong>.</li>
      <li>Pick the tracker and find the title on it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      From then on Katari updates the tracker as your progress changes, while <strong>Update tracking after progress changes</strong> in
      <Path>Settings › Tracking</Path> is on, as it is from the start. The <strong>Tracking</strong> sheet shows what the tracker
      has, but progress made on the tracker's site never marks chapters read in Katari. When you mark chapters read by hand on a title's page, <strong>Update tracking when marked finished</strong> decides whether
      the tracker follows: <strong>Always</strong>, <strong>Always ask</strong> or <strong>Never</strong>.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="enhanced" title="Trackers that follow your library by themselves">
    <p>
      Komga, Kavita and Suwayomi are servers you run, with matching sources. Log in under <strong>Enhanced trackers</strong>, and titles from
      their sources are tracked as soon as you add them to the library. Each one appears once its source is installed, and unlike
      other trackers, their progress also marks chapters read in Katari.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
